WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV — spellcheck (60s) Narrator Misha

1
00:00:00.964 --> 00:00:09.390
Twenty-dollar monthly cloud subscriptions work for a few million professionals, not seven billion everyday users.

2
00:00:11.751 --> 00:00:15.473
Spell Check is Global documents dated retail prices

3
00:00:15.473 --> 00:00:20.361
showing how standalone proofreading vanished into standard editors.

4
00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:27.563
Once the compute cost of an inline check fell below billing overhead,

5
00:00:27.563 --> 00:00:31.071
charging per check became economically irrational.

6
00:00:33.432 --> 00:00:37.963
Heavy frontier models stay metered behind paywalls precisely

7
00:00:37.963 --> 00:00:42.947
because each invocation still burns substantial datacenter energy.

8
00:00:45.308 --> 00:00:49.019
Lowering energy per verified action is not an

9
00:00:49.019 --> 00:00:53.883
afterthought—it is the economic mechanism of global access.
